cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Once the paper is published, cite the paper (preferred-citation will be updated)."
type: software
title: "Microbial Digital Library: an open, self-hosted system for managing microbial culture collections"
version: 4.7.2
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Fajoyegbe
    given-names: Emmanuel
    email: fajoyemma@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Osun State University, Osogbo, Nigeria; Beavertown Brewery, London, United Kingdom"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6089-0100"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Emmajoy5/mdl"
url: "https://emmajoy5.github.io/mdl/"
abstract: >-
  A free web application for keeping track of a laboratory culture collection. It
  records where each strain is stored, prints QR labels, works out when strains
  are due for revival, and keeps a dated history of revival checks, Gram stains
  and plate photos. Strain lists can be imported from a spreadsheet, and plate
  photos can be turned into 3D models. Each lab runs its own installation on its
  own computer or server, so its data stays with the lab.
keywords:
  - culture collection
  - strain curation
  - laboratory information management
  - brewing microbiology
  - viability monitoring
  - self-hosted software
